{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1341511-deviant-twins","id":1341511,"title":"Deviant: Twins?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-15T15:40:28-07:00","id":1341511,"title":"Deviant: Twins?","content":"Since Deviant was announced, I wanted to adapt many of my DC based CofD characters as Deviants. Some were already used by other gamelines over the course of play, but one particular pair is one I hoped would be possible via Deviant--a soul broken into two people, polar opposites, whose powers wax and wane based on the presence or lack of the other. I want to ask the community, who likely grasp Deviant's systems, if this is possible.<br /> <br /> The initial idea is that these two characters found themselves split literally in half. That their Scara and variations work in conjunction, can cancel each other out, and that each has unique powers when the other isnt present.<br /> <br /> Now i realize the Rules for Forms adds a layer. What if one twin has only Loyalty, the other has only Conviction.. the Form mechanics means that whem together they act as one in those stats, but separate, they are left on their own in terms of touch stones and what not.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, can Scars be customized so that each gains benefits when near the other and lose them when away? Can certain talents be suppressed when one is nearby? From what the system looks like, that much is possible and could be interesting to stat and play out.<br /> <br /> The idea is that Mas y Menos add to each others stats and speed etc while together, but lose a lot whem separated. But when separated, each not only gains unique powers suppressed by scars based on the other, but Form also means Mas only has Loyalty, and Menos only has Conviction.<br /> <br /> How much of this is feasible through the systems? I have access to the previews but i am still trying to grok scara and variations in general, much less deviations and forms.<br /> <br /> Any help would be appreciated, as well as other ways of portraying such &quot;twins&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T16:12:40-07:00","id":1341515,"title":"","content":"For Mas y Menos you would probably have Involuntary Stimulus, with the Stimulus being their sibling. I don't think they'd fit well as one single character.<br /> <br /> Also it's going to be easier making DC characters if you are willing to ignore and bend Deviants systems. The game isn't meant for straight superheroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:08:17-07:00","id":1341671,"title":"","content":"Power Failure is another good way to model variations that only work when the twin is or is not nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T07:02:04-07:00","id":1341850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1341511-deviant-twins?p=1341515#post1341515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mas y Menos you would probably have Involuntary Stimulus, with the Stimulus being their sibling. I don't think they'd fit well as one single character.<br /> <br /> Also it's going to be easier making DC characters if you are willing to ignore and bend Deviants systems. The game isn't meant for straight superheroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the heroes and villains in my cofdc arent deviants, just a few (MyM, Bane, Swamp Thing, and Cyborg). I even used Exalted for Superboy. But Deviant does fit some, because of how their origins could be flavored. Involuntary stimulus and power failure seem to fit pretty well, though. Deviant is so flexible, im having trouble cementing how to portray the twins, but this is a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T07:44:05-07:00","id":1341856,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of Firestorm from the Arrowverse (I'm sure he's probably also in the DC comics universe, but I'm not really familiar with DC comics.) Basically he'd have his fire powers which are only available when the two people are united as one, but then he has the multiple bodies power which would keep all of his other powers from being active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T17:39:59-07:00","id":1341972,"title":"","content":"I think you're fighting uphill to fit this into Deviant without bending it a bit (certainly not impossible, but a lot of work), but the largest conceptual sticking point here is your idea with the Anchors, which I advise against. Loyalty and Conviction aren't powers, they're <i>obsessions,</i> and having only one or the other makes for even more extreme personalities than Deviants are already designed to be. Having access to Loyalty and its Touchstones only when you're around your brother literally means your ability to love and care about and attach yourself to someone positively is directly tied to how far away your brother is, which is... strange, and probably not the story you're looking to tell.<br /> <br /> It would definitely make a lot of sense for the two characters to have each other as Loyalty Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:03:39-07:00","id":1342159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1341511-deviant-twins?p=1341972#post1341972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're fighting uphill to fit this into Deviant without bending it a bit (certainly not impossible, but a lot of work), but the largest conceptual sticking point here is your idea with the Anchors, which I advise against. Loyalty and Conviction aren't powers, they're <i>obsessions,</i> and having only one or the other makes for even more extreme personalities than Deviants are already designed to be. Having access to Loyalty and its Touchstones only when you're around your brother literally means your ability to love and care about and attach yourself to someone positively is directly tied to how far away your brother is, which is... strange, and probably not the story you're looking to tell.<br /> <br /> It would definitely make a lot of sense for the two characters to have each other as Loyalty Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. The idea behind it was that, prior to Divergence, it was one young boy that Project Cadmus (or one of the conspiracies connected to it) exposed to speed force to create a Deviant. To their surprise, when his soul fractured, they ended up with two Deviants, each with one half of the soul, polar opposites. <br /> <br /> I can see what you mean, though, as itd leave Menos a rage monster incapable of love when his brother isnt nearby, and Mas would be a nearly pasifistic friends and family kind of kid without the convictiob of his brother. In theory it sounds good, and thankfully they are NPCs and not pcs. But i see what you mean about it having mechanical issues through Anchors that could go above and beyond the story idea of a split soul. I still want to present that whole split soul vibe, as if its one character in two bodies, but there may be less... weighted ways of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}